The application must support Android, iOS, and responsive web through a shared codebase.

Do not implement a website and an unrelated mobile application. Share business logic, validation schemas, API clients, domain models, and reusable UI wherever practical.

### Backend and database

Use Supabase for:

- PostgreSQL database
- Authentication
- User profile management
- Private document storage
- Row-level security
- Database migrations
- Server-side functions or a dedicated backend for privileged operations

Use server-side API routes or Edge Functions for Gemini requests, document-processing operations, and other sensitive workflows.

Never expose the Supabase service-role key or Gemini API key in client-side code.

### AI provider

Use the Gemini Developer API through an interchangeable AI-provider abstraction.

The implementation must support:

- Server-side model selection through configuration
- Structured JSON output
- Schema validation of AI responses
- Request timeouts
- Retry and backoff policies for transient errors
- Rate limiting and usage quotas
- Error handling for unavailable models and exhausted free-tier quotas
- A provider interface that allows a different model to be integrated later

Do not assume a particular Gemini model name will remain available. Configure a supported model through an environment variable.

### Suggested repository organization

Separate the code into:

- App routes and layouts
- Reusable UI components
- Feature modules
- Domain types and validation schemas
- API client and server endpoints
- AI provider and prompts
- Database migrations and access policies
- University data ingestion and source adapters
